window.SITE={"chapters":[{"n":1,"title":"What Is Cryptography?","file":"chapter-01.html","world":1,"color":"sun","emoji":"🔐","mins":5,"secs":["s-1-1","s-1-2","s-1-3","s-1-4","s-1-5","s-1-6","s-1-7","s-1-8"],"quiz":true,"hook":"Your card number crosses café Wi-Fi, routers and a dozen strangers’ computers. So why can’t any of them read it?"},{"n":2,"title":"A Quick Trip Through History","file":"chapter-02.html","world":1,"color":"sun","emoji":"🏛️","mins":6,"secs":["s-2-1","s-2-2","s-2-3","s-2-4","s-2-5","s-2-6","s-2-7"],"quiz":true,"hook":"A cipher with 400 septillion possible keys was cracked in the 9th century, with pen and paper. How?"},{"n":3,"title":"The Math Toolbox, Gently","file":"chapter-03.html","world":1,"color":"sun","emoji":"🧮","mins":9,"secs":["s-3-1","s-3-2","s-3-3","s-3-4","s-3-5","s-3-6","s-3-7","s-3-8","s-3-9","s-3-10","s-3-11"],"quiz":true,"hook":"5⁶ mod 23 takes a split second to compute. Running it backwards, with big numbers, would outlast the universe. Welcome to the one-way street that guards the internet."},{"n":4,"title":"Randomness: The Secret Ingredient","file":"chapter-04.html","world":1,"color":"sun","emoji":"🎲","mins":5,"secs":["s-4-1","s-4-2","s-4-3","s-4-4","s-4-5"],"quiz":true,"hook":"A 256-bit key can secretly have the strength of a 15-bit one. Two deleted lines of code did exactly that to a whole operating system’s keys for two years."},{"n":5,"title":"Symmetric Encryption: One Shared Key","file":"chapter-05.html","world":2,"color":"coral","emoji":"🔑","mins":9,"secs":["s-5-1","s-5-2","s-5-3","s-5-4","s-5-5","s-5-6","s-5-7","s-5-8","s-5-9","s-5-10"],"quiz":true,"hook":"An attacker who doesn’t know the key changes “$100” into “$900”, and the bank’s decryption raises no alarm at all. How is that even possible?"},{"n":6,"title":"Hash Functions: Digital Fingerprints","file":"chapter-06.html","world":2,"color":"coral","emoji":"🫆","mins":6,"secs":["s-6-1","s-6-2","s-6-3","s-6-4","s-6-5","s-6-6","s-6-7","s-6-8","s-6-9"],"quiz":true,"hook":"Change one letter in a 4 GB movie and its fingerprint changes completely. Find two files with the same fingerprint and you can fake a Windows Update. 😱"},{"n":7,"title":"Message Authentication Codes: Tamper-Proof Seals","file":"chapter-07.html","world":2,"color":"coral","emoji":"🧷","mins":4,"secs":["s-7-1","s-7-2","s-7-3","s-7-4","s-7-5","s-7-6","s-7-7","s-7-8"],"quiz":true,"hook":"Mallory can change a message AND recompute its hash. So how does your server know a webhook really came from GitHub?"},{"n":8,"title":"Passwords and Key Derivation","file":"chapter-08.html","world":2,"color":"coral","emoji":"🧂","mins":5,"secs":["s-8-1","s-8-2","s-8-3","s-8-4","s-8-5","s-8-6","s-8-7","s-8-8","s-8-9"],"quiz":true,"hook":"Hackers just stole your website’s password database. Whether that’s a shrug or a catastrophe depends on one choice you made years ago."},{"n":9,"title":"Public-Key Cryptography: The Two-Key Revolution","file":"chapter-09.html","world":2,"color":"coral","emoji":"🗝️","mins":8,"secs":["s-9-1","s-9-2","s-9-3","s-9-4","s-9-5","s-9-6","s-9-7","s-9-8","s-9-9"],"quiz":true,"hook":"For 3,000 years, sharing a secret meant meeting first. Then someone invented a padlock anyone can snap shut, but only you can open."},{"n":10,"title":"Key Exchange: Agreeing on a Secret in Public","file":"chapter-10.html","world":2,"color":"coral","emoji":"🎨","mins":6,"secs":["s-10-1","s-10-2","s-10-3","s-10-4","s-10-5","s-10-6","s-10-7","s-10-8","s-10-9"],"quiz":true,"hook":"Two strangers shout numbers across a crowded room, and end up sharing a secret that nobody else in the room can work out."},{"n":11,"title":"Digital Signatures: Unforgeable Digital Ink","file":"chapter-11.html","world":2,"color":"coral","emoji":"✍️","mins":5,"secs":["s-11-1","s-11-2","s-11-3","s-11-4","s-11-5","s-11-6","s-11-7","s-11-8"],"quiz":true,"hook":"How can anyone on Earth check that a file came from you, without being able to forge your signature themselves?"},{"n":12,"title":"Networking Essentials for Cryptography","file":"chapter-12.html","world":3,"color":"ocean","emoji":"📮","mins":7,"secs":["s-12-1","s-12-2","s-12-3","s-12-4","s-12-5","s-12-6","s-12-7","s-12-8","s-12-9"],"quiz":true,"hook":"Your messages are chopped into postcards and passed hand to hand by 10 to 20 strangers in different countries. What can each of them read?"},{"n":13,"title":"Certificates and PKI: The Internet's ID Cards","file":"chapter-13.html","world":3,"color":"ocean","emoji":"🪪","mins":14,"secs":["s-13-1","s-13-2","s-13-3","s-13-4","s-13-5","s-13-6","s-13-7","s-13-8","s-13-9","s-13-10","s-13-11","s-13-12","s-13-13","s-13-14","s-13-15","s-13-16"],"quiz":true,"hook":"Anyone can generate a key and claim to be your bank. So who vouches that this key really belongs to bank.com?"},{"n":14,"title":"TLS and HTTPS: Putting It All Together","file":"chapter-14.html","world":3,"color":"ocean","emoji":"🤝","mins":10,"secs":["s-14-1","s-14-2","s-14-3","s-14-4","s-14-5","s-14-6","s-14-7","s-14-8","s-14-9","s-14-10","s-14-11","s-14-12","s-14-13","s-14-14","s-14-15","s-14-16"],"quiz":true,"hook":"In about 100 milliseconds, your browser and a server on another continent run almost everything from Chapters 4 to 13. Let’s watch it happen in slow motion."},{"n":15,"title":"Secure Connections: SSH, VPNs, Wi-Fi and DNS","file":"chapter-15.html","world":4,"color":"mint","emoji":"🚇","mins":8,"secs":["s-15-1","s-15-2","s-15-3","s-15-4"],"quiz":true,"hook":"SSH, VPNs, Wi-Fi and DNS look like four different worlds. Underneath, they’re the same handful of building blocks snapped together in different shapes."},{"n":16,"title":"Everyday Security: Email, Messaging, Disks, Logins and Money","file":"chapter-16.html","world":4,"color":"mint","emoji":"📱","mins":13,"secs":["s-16-1","s-16-2","s-16-3","s-16-4","s-16-5","s-16-6","s-16-7"],"quiz":true,"hook":"Your 6-digit authenticator code is an HMAC of the clock. Your passkey is a private key inside a chip. And a bitcoin is, at heart, just a signature."},{"n":17,"title":"Advanced and Emerging Cryptography","file":"chapter-17.html","world":4,"color":"mint","emoji":"⚛️","mins":10,"secs":["s-17-1","s-17-2","s-17-3","s-17-4","s-17-5","s-17-6","s-17-7"],"quiz":true,"hook":"A machine that doesn’t fully exist yet already threatens secrets you send today. Plus: how to prove you know a secret without revealing a single bit of it."},{"n":18,"title":"How Cryptography Breaks: Attacks and Pitfalls","file":"chapter-18.html","world":4,"color":"mint","emoji":"💥","mins":9,"secs":["s-18-1","s-18-2","s-18-3","s-18-4","s-18-5","s-18-6","s-18-7","s-18-8","s-18-9"],"quiz":true,"hook":"The math almost never breaks. A missing length check, one duplicated line of code, a signature made of zeros… those do."},{"n":19,"title":"Key Management: Guarding the Keys","file":"chapter-19.html","world":4,"color":"mint","emoji":"🗄️","mins":6,"secs":["s-19-1","s-19-2","s-19-3","s-19-4","s-19-5","s-19-6","s-19-7","s-19-8"],"quiz":true,"hook":"Strong crypto turns a data-protection problem into a key-protection problem. So where do you hide the one key that protects everything?"},{"n":20,"title":"Going Deeper: Proofs, Cipher Design and Crypto in Hidden Places","file":"chapter-20.html","world":5,"color":"orange","emoji":"🔭","mins":22,"secs":["s-20-1","s-20-2","s-20-3","s-20-4","s-20-5","s-20-6","s-20-7","s-20-8","s-20-9","s-20-10"],"quiz":true,"hook":"You know which tools to use. Now meet the games that define “secure”, the tricks that break ciphers, and the hidden crypto inside Tor, “Sign in with Google”, your bank card and your laptop’s boot screen."},{"n":21,"title":"Cheat Sheet: What to Use Today","file":"chapter-21.html","world":6,"color":"grape","emoji":"📋","mins":5,"secs":["s-21-1","s-21-2","s-21-3","s-21-4","s-21-5","s-21-6"],"quiz":true,"hook":"Everything you’ve learned, boiled down to one page you could stick on your fridge."},{"n":22,"title":"Glossary","file":"chapter-22.html","world":6,"color":"grape","emoji":"📖","mins":10,"secs":[],"quiz":true,"hook":"Every term in the guide, decoded. Flip the flashcards and find out how many you know cold."},{"n":"appendix","title":"Where to Learn More","file":"appendix.html","world":6,"color":"grape","emoji":"📚","mins":2,"secs":["s-books","s-courses-and-videos","s-hands-on-practice","s-trusted-references"],"quiz":false,"hook":""}],"worlds":[{"n":1,"name":"Foundations","emoji":"🏝️","color":"sun"},{"n":2,"name":"The Building Blocks","emoji":"🧱","color":"coral"},{"n":3,"name":"Trust on the Internet","emoji":"🌐","color":"ocean"},{"n":4,"name":"Crypto in the Real World","emoji":"🏙️","color":"mint"},{"n":5,"name":"Going Deeper","emoji":"🔭","color":"orange"},{"n":6,"name":"Reference","emoji":"📚","color":"grape"}],"vault":{"salt":"U6O6EPNScNJBJJYmbBESZw==","iv":"I3GCuns7ROQW+Wd6","ct":"","iter":200000,"n":22}};
